From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 09:01:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf phase 11 patch 0145 -- wave-51 asm opaque-span
 _blit_indexed lever

Per flush-instr's docs/internal/WAVE-51-ASM-BLIT-DESIGN.md (task #5
QUALIFIED GREENLIGHT): the "one untried lever" from the Latch & Plane
consultancy memo -- hand-tuned CPU-side rewrite of the `_blit_indexed`
INDEX8 colorkey blit, which carries ~6.5 ms / flip (~18-19% of
inter_flip) across BG tilelayer + FG + sprite drawcalls.

WHY DOS NEEDS THIS: the legacy colorkey path runs a per-pixel
`if (px != colorkey) dp[col] = px;` branch. On the P54C (Pentium
OverDrive 83) that branch is data-dependent and unpredictable -- every
sprite/tile edge is a ~3-4 cycle mispredict bubble -- and DJGPP GCC
12.2's Pentium U/V scheduler pairs the byte-granular conditional store
poorly. The branch cannot be hoisted at runtime without either codegen
(rejected: compiled sprites) or precomputed transparency structure.

LEVER MECHANISM (opaque-span precompute; no runtime codegen):
- At surface load, for each INDEX8 + colorkeyed source surface, scan
  every row and collapse its non-colorkey ("opaque") pixels into
  contiguous (start,len) runs -- BlitSpanTable. A fully-opaque tile
  row collapses to one run; transparency splits it into several.
- `_blit_indexed`'s colorkey path, when handed the table, no longer
  tests pixels: it intersects each precomputed run with the clipped
  source-column window and copies it via `_span_copy` -- the P54C
  `rep movsl` + 0-3 byte tail fast-string idiom. The unpredictable
  per-pixel branch is gone entirely; an opaque row becomes one
  microcoded string move.
- The win scales with opaque fraction + run contiguity: opaque-
  dominated BG tiles collapse to row memcpys; transparency-fragmented
  sprites keep short runs (smaller win). Sizing is left to the 0146
  ride-along census -- see WAVE-51-ASM-BLIT-DESIGN sec. 5.

KILLSWITCH: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_ASM_BLIT (strict "1" opt-in; default-OFF
for wave-51 per design sec. 4). Cached-at-boot static-const-bool
(blit_asm_span_enabled()) -- never a per-blit getenv. When OFF, no
span table is ever built (zero memory, zero scan cost) and
`_blit_indexed` keeps its legacy per-pixel loop byte-for-byte: the
`spans` parameter defaults to nullptr and the new fast-path branch is
`if (has_colorkey && spans)`, so OFF is a literal no-op.

CORRECTNESS REASONING:
- The span path copies exactly the non-colorkey pixels of the clipped
  region and leaves colorkey (transparent) pixels untouched -- which
  is identically what the legacy `if (px != colorkey)` loop does.
  Runs are emitted left-to-right (sorted ascending), intersected with
  the post-clip [sx, sx+cols) window; `sp`/`dp` already point at the
  clipped origin so a source column maps to one shared byte offset in
  both rows. Pixel-identical output to the legacy path.
- `_blit_indexed_mirrored` (column-reversed) is intentionally NOT
  span-converted -- it stays on its per-pixel path; mirrored blits
  are a minority of drawcalls (design sec. 1) and column reversal
  defeats contiguous-run copies.
- Span tables assume the source surface pixels are immutable after
  load. Cave Story tilesets / sprite sheets / font atlases are loaded
  once from .pbm/.png and never mutated; the table is freed + the
  build-once flag reset in Surface::cleanup() so a Tileset reload
  (delete + reload) rebuilds against new pixels.
- build_blit_span_table bails to nullptr (legacy path) on any non-
  INDEX8 / NULL-pixels / >65535-dimension surface -- run start/len
  are Uint16.

FILES (~212 LOC; ~70 substantive + ~140 comment per the essential
-correctness-doc convention):
- src/graphics/BlitSpans.h (NEW): BlitSpanRun / BlitSpanTable types +
  blit_asm_span_enabled() / build_blit_span_table() decls.
- src/graphics/Renderer.cpp: _span_copy (rep movsl primitive),
  blit_asm_span_enabled (cached gate), build_blit_span_table (load-
  time row scan), `_blit_indexed` span fast-path branch + optional
  `spans` param, 3 call-site updates (_try_fast_blit / drawTileFast /
  drawTileFastToSurface), initVideo boot banner.
- src/graphics/Surface.{h,cpp}: lazily-built _span_table member +
  spanTable() accessor; freed in cleanup().

Single-mechanism per [[single_lever_per_binary_or_else_attribution_
impossible]]: the lever is "opaque-span precompute + rep movsl blit".
NO ride-along correctness patches. NO audio code touched. The
_blit_indexed sub-decomp instrumentation is a SEPARATE env-gate in
patch 0146.

PREDICTED OUTCOME (per [[perf_measurement_discipline]] -- hypothesis,
not promise): design sec. 3 honest ceiling +2.0 to +2.5 fps if the
~6.5 ms colorkey loop is cut 35-45%; conditional on BG opaque
fraction + run contiguity, which patch 0146's census measures in the
same iter. Not a 50-fps unlock; the best available CPU-side render
lever post wave-50 NO-GO.

